Description: mesa: require geometry shader capability for desktop GL 3.2
 OpenGL 3.2 core requires geometry shaders. The GL 3.2 specification lists
 MAX_GEOMETRY_OUTPUT_VERTICES with a minimum of 256 (Table 6.42), and
 context.h (_mesa_has_geometry_shaders) assumes geometry shaders for every
 desktop context from 3.2 on. compute_version() did not check for them, so
 a driver without geometry shaders still reported 3.2 or higher as soon as
 GLSL 1.50 and the listed extensions were present. zink on a device without
 the Vulkan geometryShader feature is such a case: it advertises GLSL 4.60
 (zink_screen.c) and reports maxGeometryOutputVertices of 0 through the
 state tracker (st_extensions.c, MaxGeometryOutputVertices).
 .
 Require MaxGeometryOutputVertices >= 256 for ver_3_2. The state tracker
 fills this constant from the screen cap for every driver, and drivers with
 geometry shaders report at least 256, so they are unchanged. Without it the
 version falls back to 3.1 for core and compatibility contexts (both use
 compute_version()), the GLSL version follows to 1.40 in
 _mesa_compute_version(), and extensions such as ARB_timer_query and
 ARB_blend_func_extended stay listed. OpenGL ES is unchanged
 (OES_geometry_shader gates ES 3.2).
 .
 Only for this downstream stack; not intended for upstream submission.
